  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Reactivity with water increases on moving down the Goup from $\\mathrm{Li}$ to $\\mathrm{Cs}$ as $\\mathrm{Li} < \\mathrm{Na}$ $ < \\mathrm{K} < \\mathrm{Rb} < \\mathrm{Cs}$. This is due to increase in electropositive character. Hence Rb reacts most vigorously with water.",
